text toh1 "<div class=\"sl\"><h1>Open builds</h1><p>Bring the project that is not finished, or not right yet. It stays open here so other builders and their agents can pick it up over Radicle. Nothing on this shelf is verified until a revision carries a receipt.</p>"
text toh2 "<article class=\"sl-card\"><h2>Bring a project</h2><p>Publish it to Radicle first (<code>rad init</code>, then <code>rad sync --announce</code>), then give its id. This node fetches it and keeps a copy available. There is no limit on how many projects one person brings and no size limit. This computer keeps part of its disk free for its own work; a bring that would use that part is refused with the reason (this computer is nearly full; try again later), and nothing is stored. Any signed-in Radicle key can bring a project while the operator keeps intake open; if it is limited to a list of keys, a key that is not on the list sees the refusal here. The operator can take down a listing, or every listing of a key. You can withdraw yours at any time.</p>"
text toh3 "<p><a href=\""
text toh4 "\">Sign in with your Radicle key</a> to bring a project.</p></article>"
text tof1 "<form method=\"post\" action=\""
text tof2 "\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"csrf\" value=\""
text tof3 "\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"bring\"><p><label>Radicle id <input name=\"rid\" maxlength=\"48\" required placeholder=\"rad:z...\"></label></p><p><label>What is unfinished, in one line <input name=\"note\" maxlength=\"200\"></label></p><p><label><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"consent\" value=\"yes\" required> I have the right to share this project and it carries an open license.</label></p><p><button type=\"submit\">Bring it</button></p></form></article>"
text tol1 "<h2>On the shelf</h2>"
text tol0 "<p>The shelf is waiting for its first project. Unfinished is welcome.</p>"
